          "id": 80,
          "matching_lines": [
            "This community centers on HTTPAdapter state serialization and deserialization. HTTPAdapter GETSTATE produces the adapter attributes needed to preserve configuration, while HTTPAdapter SETSTATE consumes that state to restore the adapter, recreate proxy and configuration dictionaries, and reinitialize the pool manager. The strongest connection is the direct relationship between the two methods, with an additional relationship identifying HTTPAdapter as the component that uses SETSTATE for restoration.",
            "## HTTPAdapter SETSTATE is the central restoration component",
            "HTTPAdapter SETSTATE is described as a deserialization method that restores adapter state, recreates proxy and configuration dictionaries, and reinitializes the pool manager. This makes it the principal restoration-focused entity in the community. [Data: Entities (134)]",
